From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mason Chang <mason-cw.chang@mediatek.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 11:04:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: remove netsys v1 restriction for
 small frag check

All TX DMAs across all Netsys versions have a hardware limitation that
SDL must not be less than 16, so the Netsys version check has to be
removed.

Without this patch, the TX DMA may behave unexpectedly when processing
fragments shorter than 16 bytes.

[pesa1234 999-9925, from MediaTek's SDK. Ported to OpenWrt 6.12 for
 MilkFlint by OddBlueDog, unchanged. OpenWrt's 732-01 limited the check
 to v1 because it treated a different symptom (QDMA FIFO overflow with
 many small fragments), which MTK_RESV_BUF covers on MT7986. A GSO skb
 with a fragment under 16 bytes is now segmented in software, and a
 non-GSO skb linearized, as on v1: rare in forwarding (a GRO'd flow
 whose last segment carried under 16 bytes of payload), and the check
 itself is a walk over the fragments already in cache for mtk_tx_map().]

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c | 5 ++---
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
index 6060cfe..560b056 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -1992,7 +1992,7 @@ static bool mtk_skb_has_small_frag(struct sk_buff *skb)
 static bool mtk_skb_valid_gso(struct mtk_eth *eth, struct sk_buff *skb,
 			      unsigned int header_len)
 {
-	if (mtk_is_netsys_v1(eth) && mtk_skb_has_small_frag(skb))
+	if (mtk_skb_has_small_frag(skb))
 		return false;
 
 	if (!(skb_shinfo(skb)->gso_type & SKB_GSO_FRAGLIST))
@@ -2074,8 +2074,7 @@ static netdev_tx_t mtk_start_xmit(struct sk_buff *skb, struct net_device *dev)
 
 send:
 	skb_list_walk_safe(skb, skb, next) {
-		if ((mtk_is_netsys_v1(eth) &&
-		     mtk_skb_has_small_frag(skb) && skb_linearize(skb)) ||
+		if ((mtk_skb_has_small_frag(skb) && skb_linearize(skb)) ||
 		    mtk_tx_map(skb, dev, tx_num, ring, gso, header_len) < 0) {
 				stats->tx_dropped++;
 				dev_kfree_skb_any(skb);
